{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SYTZR1WYqHhxTLzbEWDZDm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. Re-implementations built from documentation alone diverge on edge cases. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds one package per utility; `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness; `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls; `pkg/format/` provides shared formatting. Human operator writes specs; orchestrator generates code.\n\n**Implementation State (from source_code):**\n- **Done:** `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/version`, `cmd/wc` — all have source code on the working branch\n- **Not started (specs complete):** `cmd/cat` (rel01.1), `cmd/sponge` (rel01.2), `cmd/du` (rel01.3)\n- **Deferred:** ls (rel99.0/99.1), ts (rel99.2)\n\n**Current release:** rel00.0 and rel01.0 are effectively complete (code exists). The earliest incomplete release is **rel01.1 — cat**.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nAll foundational infrastructure (rel00.0) and wc (rel01.0) have working code. The next target is **rel01.1 (cmd/cat)**. Cat has no dependencies on unbuilt packages — `pkg/testutils` exists for differential testing. Implementation must come before tests (per P2/P8). With a 1-task limit, the implementation task is the priority.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Implement cmd/cat main.go -- cat PRD: flag parsing, file concatenation, output transformations, error handling\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - \"docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate the cat PRD file named prdNNN-cat.yaml and read all requirements before implementing)\"\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel01.1-uc001-cat.yaml (cat use case defining end-to-end behavior)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.1.yaml (test suite defining expected inputs and outputs)\n      - cmd/wc/main.go (reference implementation pattern -- follow same structure for entry point, flag parsing, and error handling)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (reference for differential test pattern -- understand the binary build and DiffTest usage)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests API that cmd/cat tests will use)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/cat/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Complete cat utility implementation: flag parsing, file concatenation, output transformations, error handling\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement flag parsing for all cat flags defined in the cat PRD. Use flag.NewFlagSet('cat', flag.ContinueOnError) with fs.SetOutput(os.Stderr). Handle combination flags (-A expands to -vET, -e expands to -vE, -t expands to -vT) per the PRD. The -u flag is accepted but ignored (POSIX compatibility).\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement file concatenation: read named files in argument order and write their contents to stdout. When no file arguments are given, read from stdin. When '-' appears as a file argument, read stdin at that position in the argument list. Support interleaved file and stdin arguments.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement all output transformations specified in the cat PRD: line numbering (-n numbers all output lines starting at 1, -b numbers only non-blank lines and overrides -n), blank line squeezing (-s collapses consecutive blank lines to a single blank line), end-of-line markers (-E appends $ before each newline), TAB display (-T renders tabs as ^I), and non-printing character display (-v renders control characters as ^X notation and bytes > 127 in M- notation).\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement error handling per the cat PRD: exit 0 when all files are read successfully, exit 1 when any file cannot be opened or read. Print errors to stderr in the format 'cat: <filename>: <error>'. Continue processing remaining file arguments after encountering an error on one file.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Follow the run(args []string) int entry-point pattern from cmd/wc: main() calls os.Exit(run(os.Args[1:])), and run handles all flag parsing, I/O, and error tracking, returning the exit code.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use flag.NewFlagSet('cat', flag.ContinueOnError) with fs.SetOutput(os.Stderr) for flag parsing, matching the pattern established in cmd/wc/main.go.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Add file header with copyright (Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.), SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT, package documentation, and Implements comments referencing cat PRD requirement IDs -- matching the comment style in cmd/wc/main.go.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/cat/main.go compiles successfully with 'go build ./cmd/cat/' with no errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"All flags defined in the cat PRD are accepted by the flag parser. Unrecognized flags cause a usage message on stderr and exit code greater than 0.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"'go vet ./cmd/cat/' reports no issues.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Each function includes a comment referencing the specific cat PRD requirement it implements, using the 'Implements: prdNNN-cat RX.Y' format matching cmd/wc/main.go style.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":57364,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":57364},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dc3cbbb7-16a7-4953-a8cb-800e75fceb81","uuid":"0c67214e-b68c-45d2-b260-b7b9033fdee9"}
